.TH JSON2DIR 1 "October 2026" "json2dir-scheme 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
json2dir \- convert JSON objects to directory trees
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B json2dir
< file.json
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read one UTF-8 JSON object from standard input and materialize it in the
current directory. Command-line arguments are rejected.
.SH CONVERSION
Object keys name entries. Objects create directories; strings create files.
An array ["link", target] creates a symbolic link. An array ["script", content]
creates a file and adds all three execute bits to its default permissions.
Both array elements must be strings. All other values are rejected.
.SH BEHAVIOR
Keys must contain exactly one normal POSIX path component. Existing files
and symbolic links are unlinked before replacement. Existing directories
are reused and unrelated entries remain. Changes made before an error
are not rolled back. Entries are processed in lexical key order.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 for invalid arguments, input, or filesystem errors.
Errors are written to standard error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B GUILE
may select the Guile executable. Guile 3.0 is required.
.SH CAVEATS
Input is parsed in full before filesystem changes. JSON containers are limited
to 127 nested levels. Output files contain UTF-8 text without added newlines.
Concurrent filesystem changes and symlink races are not guarded against.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR guile (1),
.BR jq (1)
.SH AUTHORS
Scheme port of json2dir by Alan Urmancheev.
